# Noma Enterprise workspace

::summary
Noma's enterprise workspace is a modular monolith for **Docs**, **Visuals**, and **Work**, with shared identity, authorization, assets, versioning, relationships, search, notifications, changesets, and audit. This page records the in-repo kernel, hosted collaboration, PaperDOM packages, live Atlassian HTTP adapters, the AWS/EU reference stack, the independent security-review pack, and the paid-pilot usability harness.
::

## Implemented in this tree

The `EnterpriseWorkspace` kernel (`src/enterprise.ts` and `src/enterprise-*.ts`) is the executable enterprise slice. It is published on the `@ferax564/noma-cli/enterprise` subpath (Noma Cloud is on `@ferax564/noma-cli/cloud`), so the root `@ferax564/noma-cli` import stays free of `better-sqlite3`, `ws`, and `yjs`. Hosted Tiptap/Yjs, the pinned PaperDOM extract, live Atlassian HTTP, the AWS/EU CloudFormation reference, the security-review pack, and the paid-pilot usability protocol all have passing tests in this tree.

| Area | What is implemented | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Identity | OIDC adapter interface, SCIM upsert/deprovision, short-lived sessions, revocation; Noma Cloud native OpenID Connect login (PKCE, JWKS, ID-token checks, enforced-SSO policy); SAML via trusted-header proxy | `test/enterprise-workspace.test.ts`, `test/cloud-oidc.test.ts` |
| Docs | Persistent block/table IDs, lossless adapter, draft/publish coordinator, block-level three-way merge (not a CRDT) with persist-before-ack, reconnect replay, lost-ack idempotency; disjoint blocks merge, identical edits collapse, divergent edits to one block conflict; edits go through source-preserving `patchSource` | `test/stable-identity.test.ts`, `test/enterprise-merge.test.ts` |
| Hosted collab | Tiptap + Yjs over a persist-before-ack WebSocket; token via `Authorization` or `noma.bearer.*` subprotocol (query token only behind `allowQueryToken`); idle-room eviction; transactional snapshot compaction; cross-process-safe sequence allocation; server-asserted presence; read-only viewers; two real browsers; reconnect keeps acknowledged text | `test/enterprise-yjs.test.ts` |
